From ed1b64d9140f6e2c992b78bdc21a35299240e926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:25:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shop Orders: show the customer buyer

Shop orders are no longer salon-only: a customer (the app / website USER
role) buys from the same catalog through the same endpoints. A customer
order arrives with buyerType 'CUSTOMER', salon null and a customer object
{ userId, fullName, phoneNumber }.

- pages/ShopOrders.jsx: a buyerOf(order) helper (exported, so the drawer
  uses the same rule), a Buyer column that renders the salon name as
  before or the customer's name with a Customer badge and phone, a
  Buyer type filter (All / Salons / Customers) sent as buyerType, and a
  search hint that mentions salon and customer.
- components/ShopOrderDetailModal.jsx: the "Ordered by" block switches to
  the customer's name/phone with the Customer badge, the savings line
  reads Customer saved for a customer order, and the timeline understands
  the CUSTOMER actor type.
- services/communication.jsx: adminList forwards buyerType.

A row with no buyerType is treated as a salon order, so the panel can ship
before (or with) the backend migration.
